@@ -70,6 +70,22 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object to a string with ``str()``, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result followed by ``end``. Here's an example::
+
+    console.out("Hello", "World", sep=", ", style="bold")
+
+It does the following:
+
+* Writes text without pretty printing containers, so a list is written as its string form.
+* Does not wrap, crop, or fold the text.
+* Does not interpret console markup or replace emoji codes, so ``[bold]`` and ``:smiley:`` are written literally.
+* Applies highlighting by default. Pass ``highlight=False`` to turn it off, or ``highlight=None`` to use the console's highlight setting.
+* Applies a basic ``style`` in the same way as print.
+
+
